       "text": "I haven't entered the order. You confirmed the dose, but you didn't give a clinical reason for it, and I can't think of a legitimate indication for amlodipine 50 mg once daily in an adult. That is well past the 10 mg maximum, and a single dose that size could cause serious harm, including profound hypotension and shock. I'd rather not put it in the system on a confirmation alone.\n\nYou have a few ways forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily now. If the patient needs more blood pressure control, the team can add a second agent.\n- **Check for a typo or a unit mix-up.** Please look at the original order or source. A transposed or extra digit is a common cause of this kind of error.\n- **Go through pharmacy or a senior prescriber.** If there's a specialized reason for this dose, a pharmacist or attending can review it and place the order directly under your institution's high-dose override process.\n\nIf you tell me the clinical rationale, such as a specific protocol or a consultant's recommendation, I'll reconsider and can enter it with that documented in the order note. Otherwise, tell me which of the standard doses you want."
